1
00:00:00,917 --> 00:00:10,472
Welcome to the Africa capitals, episode six of six. First, I clear the chosen
names for a fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:11,135 --> 00:00:21,329
The last episode closes the series in the far south, with the three South
African capitals, the two small inland countries, and the islands of the
western Indian Ocean.

3
00:00:21,992 --> 00:00:24,627
Let's bring Windhoek into view.

4
00:00:29,654 --> 00:00:37,282
Windhoek stands in a highland basin in the middle of Namibia, with the Namib
Desert to the west and the Atlantic beyond it.

5
00:00:37,945 --> 00:00:51,633
Its name is usually read as Afrikaans for “windy corner”, though other
readings exist, and it lies on a plateau at about 1,650 metres, well inland
from the cold Atlantic coast.

6
00:00:52,291 --> 00:00:58,386
Remember the “windy corner” on its plateau, with the desert and the cold sea
to its west.

7
00:00:59,072 --> 00:01:01,197
Let's bring Gaborone into view.

8
00:01:06,071 --> 00:01:14,082
Gaborone stands in southeastern Botswana, the landlocked country between
Namibia, Zimbabwe and South Africa.

9
00:01:14,746 --> 00:01:29,166
It was a small village when it was built as the capital just before
independence in 1966, chosen so that the seat of government would lie inside
the country instead of across the border in South Africa.

10
00:01:29,830 --> 00:01:35,623
Remember the capital chosen because it was the one place inside the country
that was not on its border.

11
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:39,574
Let's bring Pretoria into view.

12
00:01:43,251 --> 00:01:49,904
Pretoria stands in the interior of South Africa, north of Johannesburg, in the
Gauteng highveld.

13
00:01:50,557 --> 00:02:00,321
It is the country’s administrative capital, and the Union Buildings behind it
were where Nelson Mandela was inaugurated as president in 1994.

14
00:02:00,982 --> 00:02:08,227
Remember the administrative capital and the Union Buildings where Mandela was
inaugurated.

15
00:02:08,898 --> 00:02:11,406
Let's bring Bloemfontein into view.

16
00:02:15,730 --> 00:02:21,825
Bloemfontein stands in the centre of South Africa, and it is the country’s
judicial capital.

17
00:02:22,491 --> 00:02:33,451
The country’s Supreme Court of Appeal sits here, and the National Women’s
Memorial records the Afrikaner families who took refuge in the city during the
Boer War.

18
00:02:34,114 --> 00:02:43,065
Remember the judicial capital whose name means fountain of flowers, where
Tolkien was born in 1892.

19
00:02:43,747 --> 00:02:45,965
Let's bring Cape Town into view.

20
00:02:50,624 --> 00:02:58,043
Cape Town stands on the Atlantic coast at the south-western corner of Africa,
with Table Mountain rising directly behind it.

21
00:02:58,693 --> 00:03:07,609
It is South Africa’s legislative capital and the seat of the national
Parliament, and the mountain behind it is one of the oldest on the continent.

22
00:03:08,274 --> 00:03:14,288
Remember the legislative capital under Table Mountain, at the far
south-western corner.

23
00:03:14,963 --> 00:03:17,343
Let's bring Mbabane into view.

24
00:03:21,712 --> 00:03:31,731
Mbabane stands in the western highveld of Eswatini, the small country the map
labels eSwatini, between South Africa and Mozambique.

25
00:03:32,392 --> 00:03:43,224
The country took the name eSwatini in 2018, and the capital stands in its own
western uplands, with the royal centre at Lobamba to the west.

26
00:03:43,877 --> 00:03:49,589
Remember the highveld capital of eSwatini, the renamed country the map labels
for you.

27
00:03:50,278 --> 00:03:53,169
Let's bring Maseru into view.

28
00:03:57,147 --> 00:04:04,392
Maseru stands on the Caledon River, in the west of Lesotho, the country
entirely surrounded by South Africa.

29
00:04:05,046 --> 00:04:17,504
Lesotho is the only country in the world with no border to any other country
except one, and its capital is the gateway from the South African plateau into
the mountains.

30
00:04:18,172 --> 00:04:24,732
Remember the only country completely inside another one, with its capital on
the Caledon River.

31
00:04:25,495 --> 00:04:28,130
Let's bring Antananarivo into view.

32
00:04:37,850 --> 00:04:47,440
Antananarivo stands in the highlands of Madagascar, on the central plateau
above the rice paddies, with the Indian Ocean far to the east.

33
00:04:48,097 --> 00:04:58,465
Its name is read as “city of the thousand”, for the thousand soldiers said to
have guarded it, and the Rova, the palace of its kings and queens, stands on
its highest hill.

34
00:04:59,116 --> 00:05:06,616
Remember the city of a thousand on the hills of Madagascar, with the kings’
palace on the highest of them.

35
00:05:07,385 --> 00:05:09,510
Let's bring Moroni into view.

36
00:05:16,531 --> 00:05:25,912
Moroni stands on Grande Comore, the largest island of the Comoros, in the
Mozambique Channel between Mozambique and Madagascar.

37
00:05:26,566 --> 00:05:34,542
It stands at the foot of the Karthala, one of the world’s largest active
volcanoes, which fills about half of the island.

38
00:05:35,207 --> 00:05:41,685
Remember the capital beside a volcano that fills half its island, north of
Madagascar.

39
00:05:42,373 --> 00:05:44,498
Let's bring São Tomé into view.

40
00:05:49,198 --> 00:05:56,745
São Tomé stands on the island of the same name, on the equator in the Gulf of
Guinea, off the coast of Gabon.

41
00:05:57,399 --> 00:06:11,819
The fort of São Sebastião, of 1575, now serves as the national museum, and
early in the twentieth century these islands were the largest cocoa producer
in the world.

42
00:06:12,470 --> 00:06:19,076
Remember the equatorial island capital in the Gulf of Guinea, whose cocoa
islands once led the world.

43
00:06:24,898 --> 00:06:45,346
Windhoek keeps the hot springs in its highland basin, Gaborone was chosen
because it lay inside Botswana rather than on its border, and South Africa
shows three capitals at once: Pretoria to administer, Bloemfontein to judge,
Cape Town to legislate under Table Mountain.

44
00:06:45,999 --> 00:07:02,775
Remember the highveld capital of eSwatini at Mbabane, the country inside a
country at Maseru, the highland capital of Madagascar at Antananarivo, the
volcano island at Moroni, and the equatorial island capital at São Tomé.
